outputs.ts's ExitCodeOptions doc comment and transport.ts's finalize() implement the same invariant: no stdout is ever written on the stderr/BLOCK(2) exit path, because Claude Code's hook-result parser treats any stdout that parses as valid JSON as success regardless of exit code. The equivalent span carried forward from `claude-code-hooks/exit-code-block-no-stdout`; the doc half now anchors the hub skill's Claude Code reference template under skills-src, the source the four platform trees are built from, while the package README documents the same invariant without being anchored here.
